.TH 3DS2APPLE-BUILDER 1 "2026-11-12" "3ds2apple-builder 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
3ds2apple-builder \- Linux frontend for the 3ds2apple Builder
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B 3ds2apple-builder
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fICOMMAND\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B 3ds2apple-builder
builds one legally owned, decrypted Nintendo 3DS ROM into an unsigned iOS app
(IPA) on a macOS host that the user controls: a local macOS VM, a Mac on the
LAN, or a cloud Mac. The heavy AOT pipeline (3dsrecomp, Apple's clang,
xcodebuild) runs on that macOS host through the 3ds2apple Build Agent.
.PP
The frontend is a Linux-specific layer over the shared
.B zkb
client. It finds a local QEMU/KVM macOS VM's forwarded SSH port, pairs the host
with an SSH key (never a password), streams one build, re-verifies the
downloaded IPA against the Agent's manifest, and prints the manual
signing/installation steps.
.PP
It never signs, installs or distributes anything, never asks for an Apple ID,
UDID, certificate or provisioning profile, and never contacts a
project-operated server. The ROM goes only to the configured macOS host and is
deleted there when the build ends (unless the user explicitly keeps it).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-zkb " " \fIPATH\fR
Path of the shared
.B zkb
client. Default: \fB$ZKB_BIN\fR, a sibling of this binary, then \fB$PATH\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-config " " \fIPATH\fR
Builder configuration file. Default: the shared client's location
(\fB$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/3ds2apple/builder/config.toml\fR or
\fB$ZKB_CONFIG_DIR/config.toml\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-json
Machine-readable output: JSON for this frontend's commands, NDJSON from the
shared client.
.TP
.B \-\-no-input
Never prompt. Choices that would need an answer become usage errors.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Show the shared client, configured hosts, detected macOS VM endpoints and the
next commands. This is also what runs with no command.
.TP
.BIR vm " " discover
List candidate SSH endpoints from \fB$ZKB_VM_*\fR, QEMU/KVM \fBhostfwd\fR rules
and \fB127.0.0.1\fR ports that answer with an SSH banner.
.TP
.BR vm " " setup " " \-\-name \fINAME\fR [\-\-host \fIHOST\fR \-\-port \fIPORT\fR] [\-\-user \fIUSER\fR] [\-\-key \fIPATH\fR] [\-\-yes | \-\-fingerprint \fISHA256:...\fR] [\-\-test]
Discover or accept an endpoint, show the host-key fingerprint, and pair the
host through the shared client. Pairing uses a dedicated SSH key; the key's
\fBauthorized_keys\fR line is printed for the user to add on the Mac.
\fB--test\fR runs the host self-test right after pairing; it succeeds once the
printed line has been added.
.TP
.BR build " " [\-\-host \fINAME\fR] [\-\-rom \fIPATH\fR] [\-\-out \fIDIR\fR] [options]
Select a ROM (prompted for when omitted in a terminal), run the shared build
on the macOS host, stream the log, download the IPA, re-hash it and print the
result plus the installation guidance. Other options mirror
.BR "\fBzkb build\fR" :
\fB\-\-name\fR, \fB\-\-display\-name\fR, \fB\-\-bundle\-id\fR,
\fB\-\-title\-id\fR, \fB\-\-no\-moltenvk\fR, \fB\-\-hardware\-renderer\fR,
\fB\-\-clean\fR, \fB\-\-keep\-input\fR, \fB\-\-expected\-revision\fR,
\fB\-\-no\-download\fR, \fB\-\-allow\-any\-file\fR, \fB\-\-rom\-dir\fR.
.TP
.BR doctor " " [\-\-host \fINAME\fR] [\-\-probe]
Check the shared client, OpenSSH tools, configuration and key permissions,
detected VM endpoints and the data directory. With \fB--host\fR it also runs
the remote \fBzkb host test\fR. Exit status 3 when a check fails.
.TP
.BR install-guide " " [\-\-ipa \fIPATH\fR]
Print the signing and installation instructions. With \fB--ipa\fR the artifact's
size and SHA256 are filled in and hashed locally.
.TP
.BR zkb " " \fIARGS\fR...
Run the shared client with the given arguments (passthrough), for example
\fB3ds2apple-builder zkb host list\fR. The shared client's exit code is
preserved.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ZKB_VM_SSH
Endpoint override, \fB[user@]host[:port]\fR (highest priority).
.TP
.B ZKB_VM_HOST, ZKB_VM_PORT, ZKB_VM_USER
Individual endpoint overrides used when \fBZKB_VM_SSH\fR is unset.
.TP
.B ZKB_VM_KEY
Existing private key to use instead of a dedicated one.
.TP
.B ZKB_BIN
Path of the shared \fBzkb\fR client.
.TP
.B ZKB_CONFIG_DIR, ZKB_DATA_DIR
Override the shared client's configuration and data directories.
.TP
.B ZKB_ROM_DIR
Extra directory searched for \fB.3ds\fR/\fB.cci\fR files.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 success; 1 the build failed; 2 usage or configuration error; 3 the macOS
host, connection or Agent failed; 4 canceled; 5 local I/O error; 64 internal
error.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/3ds2apple/builder/config.toml
Host profiles (SSH key paths, profile-private \fBknown_hosts\fR). No password is
ever stored.
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/3ds2apple/builder/artifacts/
Downloaded IPAs by default.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
# Pair the local CachyOS macOS VM (QEMU forwards host :2222 to guest :22)
3ds2apple-builder vm setup --name cachyos-vm

# Build a ROM you own and verify the download
3ds2apple-builder build --host cachyos-vm --rom ~/ROM/"Pokemon Y.cci"

# Read the signing/installation steps
3ds2apple-builder install-guide --ipa \\
  ~/.local/share/3ds2apple/builder/artifacts/pokemon-y/pokemon-y-AOT.ipa
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zkb (1),
.I https://github.com/HFYKratos/3ds2apple
.PP
The macOS host runs
.B builder-agent
(builder/README.md). The per-game AOT pipeline is documented in
.I scripts/AOT_BUILD.md
and
.I docs/build.md
in the source repository.
.SH SECURITY
Only use decrypted ROMs you legally own. The unsigned IPA contains code derived
from the game: sign it yourself with Sideloadly/AltStore on a Windows or macOS
machine and do not redistribute it. The project provides no ROM, keys or
download service.
